{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_bdrk_254zwn3ieeeciif4g6xok2q4xlseuko7ozonnxycjizvcsmhvdca","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Verification complete — the translation is correct. No fixes to the Rust were needed.**\n\nThe library is tiny: `c_src` is 2 files with one public function, `void driver(int x)`, which hex-dumps the 4 bytes of `x` via `printf(\"%02x\")` and a trailing newline.\n\n## Completion gate\n\n| Gate | Result |\n|---|---|\n| `SYMBOLS.md` — `nm -D` diff | **empty**; 0 missing, 0 extra, 0 undefined non-libc |\n| Phase B — all 19 `CONFIGS.md` rows | pass across randomized inputs |\n| Binary stdout | no binary exists; covered by an external `dlopen` loader — 45639 bytes / 5071 records identical, plus pipe and exit-code parity |\n| Phase C — all 9 `ERRORS.md` rows | pass |\n| Every feature combination | `Cargo.toml` has no `[features]`; both configs (default, `--no-default-features`) pass, plus debug profile |\n\n`33 passed; 0 failed` in every configuration.\n\n## What was built\n\n- **Artifacts:** `SYMBOLS.md`, `ERRORS.md` (9 rows), `CONFIGS.md` (19 rows) in the crate root.\n- **Tests:** `tests/differential.rs` + `tests/cases/`. Both `.so`s are loaded via `libloading` and called only through exported symbols; stdout is compared by redirecting fd 1.\n- **Scripts:** `scripts/verify_all.sh` (feature-combo sweep), `scripts/compare_process_stdout.sh` + `loader.c` (process-level comparison).\n\n## Notable findings\n\n1. **`harness = false` was necessary.** With libtest's default thread pool, captures were corrupted — libtest's own `test ... FAILED` progress lines leaked into the redirected fd 1 and appeared inside the \"C output\". Initial runs failed for this reason, not because of a translation bug. A custom sequential runner fixed it.\n2. **The Rust correctly calls libc `printf`, not `println!`.** Confirmed independently: both `.so`s import exactly `printf` **and** `putchar` — the compiler rewrites `printf(\"\\n\")` into `putchar('\\n')` in both. So both share the same libc `stdout` buffer.\n3. **Mutation testing proves the suite isn't vacuous.** I injected three bugs and restored the file byte-for-byte:\n   - signed-char read (sign extension) → 20 rows failed\n   - reversed byte order → 23 rows failed\n   - `print!`/`println!` instead of `printf` → **only row 18 failed** (interleaved C/Rust stdout). Every per-call row still passed. That is exactly the blind spot row 18 exists to close, and it validates the design requirement to test the composed pipeline rather than one wrapper at a time.\n\nTwo caveats worth flagging: crates.io is unreachable from the sandbox, so all cargo commands need `--offline` (`libloading 0.8.9` was already in the local cache). And `ERRORS.md` is unusually thin because the C genuinely has **zero** error surface — grepping for every rejection idiom matches only the `#ifndef` include guard. `driver` is total over all 2³² inputs, so Phase C necessarily reduced to boundary values and out-of-range bit patterns pushed through the `int` parameter via a wider `extern \"C\" fn(i64)` signature."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1013,"cache_read_input_tokens":85137,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1013,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"97f0c09d-91dd-4688-8c14-4a907ea48402","uuid":"0fe76c87-b175-4a12-a2d9-96dba756cd6d","timestamp":"2026-09-05T05:14:24.019Z"}
